{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>What</b> — as if the poet asks them: why is this?" "And the sense of <b>that you flee</b> — that it turned into parched land and the waters dried up." "And the sense of <b>the mountains</b> — it is the one who turns the rock into a pool of water. And in the verse \"the mountains and all hills,\" I will explain the difference between them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 114, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:38.457354692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}